C RS
"Direction 2 (C11 forbids, C++20 allows) -- the genuine test. A release store on f
 is followed by a RELAXED store of 2 to f by the SAME thread; the reader acquires f
 and observes 2. Under C++11/14/17 that relaxed store is part of the RELEASE
 SEQUENCE headed by the release store, so an acquire that reads it synchronises with
 the release and the data write happens-before the data read: (1:r0=2, 1:r1=0) is
 FORBIDDEN. herd7 -model c11_orig.cat => Never (verified). C++20 weakened release
 sequences (P0982): only RMWs -- not later same-thread relaxed stores -- continue
 them, so reading 2 carries no release and the stale read is ALLOWED. The C++20
 side is shown by the companion RS+cpp20.litmus."
{ int data=0; int f=0; }
P0 (int* data, atomic_int* f) {
  *data = 1;
  atomic_store_explicit(f,1,memory_order_release);
  atomic_store_explicit(f,2,memory_order_relaxed);
}
P1 (int* data, atomic_int* f) {
  int r0 = atomic_load_explicit(f,memory_order_acquire);
  int r1 = *data;
}
exists (1:r0=2 /\ 1:r1=0)
